# 316 - Clustered Worldserver Architecture

Distribute AzerothCore worldserver across multiple machines. Each node handles
a portion of the world, with coordination for cross-node interactions.

## Current Behavior

Single worldserver process handles everything:
- All maps, zones, instances
- All players, NPCs, creatures
- All combat, spells, movement
- All database operations
- Single point of failure, single machine's resources

## Intended Behavior

Worldserver functionality distributed across a cluster:
- Multiple nodes share the load
- Nodes communicate for cross-boundary interactions
- Failure of one node doesn't crash the world
- Horizontal scaling: add nodes to handle more players

