### Distributable vs Centralized

| Component | Distributable? | Notes |
|-----------|---------------|-------|
| Maps/Zones | YES | Natural partition boundary |
| Instances | YES | Isolated, spawn on any node |
| Battlegrounds | YES | Isolated, spawn on any node |
| Player Sessions | YES | Follow player's current zone |
| Creature AI | YES | Local to zone |
| Combat/Spells | PARTIAL | Local when same-zone, complex when cross-zone |
| Groups/Raids | PARTIAL | Members may span zones |
| Guilds | CENTRALIZED | Global state, infrequent updates |
| Auction House | CENTRALIZED | Global state, transactional |
| Mail | CENTRALIZED | Global state, async delivery |
| Chat Channels | PARTIAL | Some global, some zone-local |
| Database | CENTRALIZED | Single source of truth |

## Architecture Options

### Option A: Zone-Based Sharding

Each node owns specific zones. Players transfer between nodes when crossing zones.

```
┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐
│     NODE A      │     │     NODE B      │     │     NODE C      │
│                 │     │                 │     │                 │
│  Eastern        │     │  Kalimdor       │     │  Northrend      │
│  Kingdoms       │     │                 │     │                 │
│                 │     │                 │     │                 │
│  - Elwynn       │     │  - Durotar      │     │  - Borean       │
│  - Westfall     │     │  - Barrens      │     │  - Howling      │
│  - Redridge     │     │  - Ashenvale    │     │  - Dragonblight │
│  - ...          │     │  - ...          │     │  - ...          │
└────────┬────────┘     └────────┬────────┘     └────────┬────────┘
         │                       │                       │
         └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘
                                 │
                    ┌────────────┴────────────┐
                    │     COORDINATOR         │
                    │                         │
                    │  - Player registry      │
                    │  - Zone ownership       │
                    │  - Cross-node routing   │
                    │  - Global services      │
                    └────────────┬────────────┘
                                 │
                    ┌────────────┴────────────┐
                    │       DATABASE          │
                    │                         │
                    │  - Characters           │
                    │  - Guilds               │
                    │  - Auction              │
                    └─────────────────────────┘
```

**Pros:**
- Clear ownership boundaries
- Minimal cross-node communication within a zone
- Matches game's natural structure

**Cons:**
- Uneven load (popular zones vs empty zones)
- Zone transitions require handoff
- Some zones are much larger than others

### Option B: Grid-Based Sharding

Divide the world into a grid. Each node owns grid cells regardless of zone.

```
